<title>SINGAPORE: International Factors net up 21 pct.</title>
<headline>International Factors net up 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 4.93	vs   4.06</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		 3.00	vs   3.00</p>
<p>    Special dividend (cents)     2.00	vs    nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		4.90	vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Gross operating income	30.71	vs  24.94</p>
<p>    Investment income		1.90	vs   2.02</p>
<p>    Other income		     0.23	vs   0.41</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	     9.76	vs   9.40</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation    3.33	vs   2.13</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	2.97	vs   2.81</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   5.68	vs   4.07</p>
<p>    Tax				  3.72	vs   2.82</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	(gain)  0.65	vs   0.22 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - International Factors (Singapore) Ltd is a finance and factoring company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
